<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112546" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῠλᾰκ-τήριος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>serving as a protection,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ περί τι φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Lg.</u>
					842d
				</span></i>
			, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῠλά̆κ-της</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ου</span>, ὁ, <i>one who
				preserves,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν ἰδίων ἐθῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ph.
					2.577
				</span></i>
			 (pl.), sed leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τικοί.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φυλακτήρ</span>
			, a magistrate at Cumae, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.291f
			</span></i>.</div>
